for (i = 0; i < 200; i = i + 2) 
{
    if (z > i) 
    {
        p = p + x + 3;
        q = q + y-> f1;
    } else 
    {
        p = p + y-> f2;
        q = q + x + 3;
    }
}</pre></code>Assume that the variable y points to a struct (allocated on the heap) containing two fields f1 and f2, and the local variables x, y, z, p, q, and i are allotted registers. Common sub-expression elimination (CSE) optimization is applied on the code. The number of addition and the dereference operations (of the form  y -> f1 or y -> f2) in the optimized code, respectively, are:

